       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. There's no dosing regimen where 16,000 mg/day of ibuprofen is therapeutic. It's well into the range where toxicity is expected, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS effects. A single 4000 mg dose is already above the maximum daily dose. I'd be putting a patient at serious risk, and confirming the order doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Correct the dose.** I can enter 400 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO three or four times daily. Either takes seconds.\n- **Escalate if you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect.** A pharmacist or your attending can help with other options, such as scheduled acetaminophen, a different NSAID, or a multimodal regimen.\n- **Check for a unit or entry error.** If the intended dose was 400 mg, or 4000 mg total per day, I can enter the correct amount.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
